 all the earth!","verse":9}],"id":"Lord","label":"LORD","matchReviews":[{"ruleId":"Lord::LORD::reviewed_capitalized_divine_title","scope":"reviewed_capitalized_divine_title","senseReview":"Only literal uppercase LORD is admitted globally. Source Lord article explicitly covers God as Lord; lowercase human lord and sentence-title Lord are not inferred from this rule.","sourceHeadwordId":"Lord","term":"LORD"}],"matchingRule":"reviewed_exact_headword","matchingRules":["reviewed_exact_headword"],"sourceProvenanceId":"Lord","sourceTitle":"Lord"}],"format":"bsb-study-chapter-v2","notes":[{"chapterAssociationStatus":"canonical_reference","content":[{"c":[{"c":[{"href":"?bref=Ps.8.1-9","r":"Ps.8.1-9","rawR":"Ps.8.1-9","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.8.1-9","value":"Ps.8.1-9"}],"t":"ref","v":"Ps 8"}],"sourceClass":"sn-ref","t":"span"}," ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.8.1-9","r":"Ps.8.1-9","rawR":"Ps.8.1-9","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.8.1-9","value":"Ps.8.1-9"}],"t":"ref","v":"Psalm 8"}," opens the second segment of Book One (",{"href":"?bref=Ps.8.1-14.7","r":"Ps.8.1-14.7","rawR":"Ps.8.1-14.7","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.8.1-14.7","value":"Ps.8.1-14.7"}],"t":"ref","v":"Pss 8–14"},"). The psalmist celebrates God’s creation and the dignity of the ideal human being (see ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.1.1-6","r":"Ps.1.1-6","rawR":"Ps.1.1-6","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.1.1-6","value":"Ps.1.1-6"}],"t":"ref","v":"Ps 1"},"). Instead of the world of enemies, wicked people, and distorted justice that is presented in ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.3.1-7.17","r":"Ps.3.1-7.17","rawR":"Ps.3.1-7.17","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.3.1-7.17","value":"Ps.3.1-7.17"}],"t":"ref","v":"Pss 3–7"},", this psalm promotes an image of the world as God originally created it. A weary person can envision a place of dignity in God’s world."],"sourceClass":"sn-text","t":"p"}],"id":"StudyNote:Ps.8.1-9","refs":[{"book":"PSA","endChapter":8,"endVerse":9,"startChapter":8,"startVerse":1}],"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Ps.8.1-9","product":"TyndaleOpenStudyNotes","typename":"StudyNote"},"sourceBookAppCode":"PSA","sourceChapterCoverage":[8],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"1a5fd9f3af10539920acad0743fa6a715d9ee8015264c37c5ae7f2c91ded0599","sourceItemName":"Ps.8.1-9","sourceMember":"Tyndale Open Study Notes/StudyNotes.xml","sourceOrder":6031,"sourceReferenceException":false,"sourceReferenceMappingEvidence":{"appCode":"PSA","canonicalOSIS":"Ps","method":"official_book_intro_ref_title","sourceOSIS":"Ps"},"sourceReferenceStatus":"canonical","sourceRefsExact":"Ps.8.1-9","sourceRelease":"1.25","sourceTitleExact":null,"supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[],"title":"Ps.8.1-9","type":"StudyNote"},{"chapterAssociationStatus":"canonical_reference","content":[{"c":[{"c":[{"href":"?bref=Ps.8.1","r":"Ps.8.1","rawR":"Ps.8.1","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.8.1","value":"Ps.8.1"}],"t":"ref","v":"8:1"}],"sourceClass":"sn-ref","t":"span"}," The ",{"c":["Lord"],"sourceClass":"sn-excerpt-divine-name","t":"span"}," (Hebrew ",{"c":["Yahweh"],"sourceClass":"hebrew","t":"span"},"), the covenant God of Israel (",{"href":"?bref=Exod.3.15","r":"Exod.3.15","rawR":"Exod.3.15","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Exod.3.15","value":"Exod.3.15"}],"t":"ref","v":"Exod 3:15"},"), also holds the title of ",{"c":["Lord"],"sourceClass":"sn-excerpt","t":"span"}," (Hebrew ",{"c":["’adonay"],"sourceClass":"hebrew","t":"span"},"), the king of the earth. • The word translated ",{"c":["majestic"],"sourceClass":"sn-excerpt","t":"span"}," (sometimes translated “mighty”) can describe kings (",{"href":"?bref=Ps.136.18","r":"Ps.136.18","rawR":"Ps.136.18","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.136.18","value":"Ps.136.18"}],"t":"ref","v":"Ps 136:18"},"), heroes (",{"href":"?bref=Ps.16.3","r":"Ps.16.3","rawR":"Ps.16.3","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.16.3","value":"Ps.16.3"}],"t":"ref","v":"16:3"},"), mountains (",{"href":"?bref=Ps.76.4","r":"Ps.76.4","rawR":"Ps.76.4","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.76.4","value":"Ps.76.4"}],"t":"ref","v":"76:4"},"), or waves breaking on the seashore (",{"href":"?bref=Ps.93.4","r":"Ps.93.4","rawR":"Ps.93.4","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.93.4","value":"Ps.93.4"}],"t":"ref","v":"93:4"},"). While all are awe-inspiring and mighty, the created order pales in comparison with the Lord. • A person’s ",{"c":["name"],"sourceClass":"sn-excerpt","t":"span"}," embodies their reputation. • ",{"c":["The earth"],"sourceClass":"sn-excerpt","t":"span"}," and ",{"c":["the heavens"],"sourceClass":"sn-excerpt","t":"span"}," reveal the Lord’s splendor. All creation worships and praises the Lord (",{"href":"?bref=Ps.66.4","r":"Ps.66.4","rawR":"Ps.66.4","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.66.4","value":"Ps.66.4"}],"t":"ref","v":"66:4"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.113.3","r":"Ps.113.3","rawR":"Ps.113.3","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.113.3","value":"Ps.113.3"}],"t":"ref","v":"113:3"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.145.21","r":"Ps.145.21","rawR":"Ps.145.21","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.145.21","value":"Ps.145.21"}],"t":"ref","v":"145:21"},")."],"sourceClass":"sn-text","t":"p"}],"id":"StudyNote:Ps.8.1","refs":[{"book":"PSA","endChapter":8,"endVerse":1,"startChapter":8,"startVerse":1}],"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Ps.8.1","product":"TyndaleOpenStudyNotes","typename":"StudyNote"},"sourceBookAppCode":"PSA","sourceChapterCoverage":[8],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"f7a79ad28dd7f397786e7b935f980054952099bd86ed93697a9fbe5120f3dc27","sourceItemName":"Ps.8.1","sourceMember":"Tyndale Open Study Notes/StudyNotes.xml","sourceOrder":6032,"sourceReferenceException":false,"sourceReferenceMappingEvidence":{"appCode":"PSA","canonicalOSIS":"Ps","method":"official_book_intro_ref_title","sourceOSIS":"Ps"},"sourceReferenceStatus":"canonical","sourceRefsExact":"Ps.8.1","sourceRelease":"1.25","sourceTitleExact":null,"supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[],"title":"Ps.8.1","type":"StudyNote"},{"chapterAssociationStatus":"canonical_reference","content":[{"c":[{"c":[{"href":"?bref=Ps.8.2","r":"Ps.8.2","rawR":"Ps.8.2","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.8.2","value":"Ps.8.2"}],"t":"ref","v":"8:2"}],"sourceClass":"sn-ref","t":"span"}," ",{"c":["silencing:"],"sourceClass":"sn-excerpt","t":"span"}," The loud noise of the oppressors contrasts with the praise of God. In the end, the praise of God will overwhelm the sound of evil (",{"href":"?bref=Ps.31.18","r":"Ps.31.18","rawR":"Ps.31.18","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.31.18","value":"Ps.31.18"}],"t":"ref","v":"31:18"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.63.11","r":"Ps.63.11","rawR":"Ps.63.11","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.63.11","value":"Ps.63.11"}],"t":"ref","v":"63:11"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.101.5","r":"Ps.101.5","rawR":"Ps.101.5","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.101.5","value":"Ps.101.5"}],"t":"ref","v":"101:5"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.143.12","r":"Ps.143.12","rawR":"Ps.143.12","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.143.12","value":"Ps.143.12"}],"t":"ref","v":"143:12"},"). • Those who ",{"c":["oppose"],"sourceClass":"sn-excerpt","t":"span"}," God seethe with vindictive anger (",{"href":"?bref=Ps.2.1-3","r":"Ps.2.1-3","rawR":"Ps.2.1-3","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.2.1-3","value":"Ps.2.1-3"}],"t":"ref","v":"2:1-3"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.44.16","r":"Ps.44.16","rawR":"Ps.44.16","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.44.16","value":"Ps.44.16"}],"t":"ref","v":"44:16"},"; cp. ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.149.6-7","r":"Ps.149.6-7","rawR":"Ps.149.6-7","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.149.6-7","value":"Ps.149.6-7"}],"t":"ref","v":"149:6-7"},")."],"sourceClass":"sn-text","t":"p"}],"id":"StudyNote:Ps.8.2","refs":[{"book":"PSA","endChapter":8,"endVerse":2,"startChapter":8,"startVerse":2}],"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Ps.8.2","product":"TyndaleOpenStudyNotes","typename":"StudyNote"},"sourceBookAppCode":"PSA","sourceChapterCoverage":[8],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"e7bb1d5f5b8659928f38669064b4ddaab2a52a1b51db1815561150b9bf0c4ae4","sourceItemName":"Ps.8.2","sourceMember":"Tyndale Open Study Notes/StudyNotes.xml","sourceOrder":6033,"sourceReferenceException":false,"sourceReferenceMappingEvidence":{"appCode":"PSA","canonicalOSIS":"Ps","method":"official_book_intro_ref_title","sourceOSIS":"Ps"},"sourceReferenceStatus":"canonical","sourceRefsExact":"Ps.8.2","sourceRelease":"1.25","sourceTitleExact":null,"supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[],"title":"Ps.8.2","type":"StudyNote"},{"chapterAssociationStatus":"canonical_reference","content":[{"c":[{"c":[{"href":"?bref=Ps.8.3-5","r":"Ps.8.3-5","rawR":"Ps.8.3-5","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.8.3-5","value":"Ps.8.3-5"}],"t":"ref","v":"8:3-5"}],"sourceClass":"sn-ref","t":"span"}," In light of God’s awesome glory, it might seem that people would be insignificant to him. However, he has ",{"c":["crowned them with glory and honor"],"sourceClass":"sn-excerpt","t":"span"}," and placed them over all creation."],"sourceClass":"sn-text","t":"p"}],"id":"StudyNote:Ps.8.3-5","refs":[{"book":"PSA","endChapter":8,"endVerse":5,"startChapter":8,"startVerse":3}],"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Ps.8.3-5","product":"TyndaleOpenStudyNotes","typename":"StudyNote"},"sourceBookAppCode":"PSA","sourceChapterCoverage":[8],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"7d359d86d7eace53a3904f8875bdb00cadfdc6b2e3b47788ba0c8cd56f3edcf1","sourceItemName":"Ps.8.3-5","sourceMember":"Tyndale Open Study Notes/StudyNotes.xml","sourceOrder":6034,"sourceReferenceException":false,"sourceReferenceMappingEvidence":{"appCode":"PSA","canonicalOSIS":"Ps","method":"official_book_intro_ref_title","sourceOSIS":"Ps"},"sourceReferenceStatus":"canonical","sourceRefsExact":"Ps.8.3-5","sourceRelease":"1.25","sourceTitleExact":null,"supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[],"title":"Ps.8.3-5","type":"StudyNote"},{"chapterAssociationStatus":"canonical_reference","content":[{"c":[{"c":[{"href":"?bref=Ps.8.3","r":"Ps.8.3","rawR":"Ps.8.3","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.8.3","value":"Ps.8.3"}],"t":"ref","v":"8:3"}],"sourceClass":"sn-ref","t":"span"}," The nations around Israel worshiped heavenly objects as deities. The sun, ",{"c":["moon"],"sourceClass":"sn-excerpt","t":"span"},{"c":[","],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"}," and ",{"c":["stars"],"sourceClass":"sn-excerpt","t":"span"}," are indeed immense and glorious, but they are merely ",{"c":["the work of your fingers,"],"sourceClass":"sn-excerpt","t":"span"}," a reason to praise the Almighty."],"sourceClass":"sn-text","t":"p"}],"id":"StudyNote:Ps.8.3","refs":[{"book":"PSA","endChapter":8,"endVerse":3,"startChapter":8,"startVerse":3}],"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Ps.8.3","product":"TyndaleOpenStudyNotes","typename":"StudyNote"},"sourceBookAppCode":"PSA","sourceChapterCoverage":[8],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"3410538bc129871c1e828a88f87c3f701e303ea92e3ab934f51a69e6220db3c1","sourceItemName":"Ps.8.3","sourceMember":"Tyndale Open Study Notes/StudyNotes.xml","sourceOrder":6035,"sourceReferenceException":false,"sourceReferenceMappingEvidence":{"appCode":"PSA","canonicalOSIS":"Ps","method":"official_book_intro_ref_title","sourceOSIS":"Ps"},"sourceReferenceStatus":"canonical","sourceRefsExact":"Ps.8.3","sourceRelease":"1.25","sourceTitleExact":null,"supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[],"title":"Ps.8.3","type":"StudyNote"},{"chapterAssociationStatus":"canonical_reference","content":[{"c":[{"c":[{"href":"?bref=Ps.8.4","r":"Ps.8.4","rawR":"Ps.8.4","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.8.4","value":"Ps.8.4"}],"t":"ref","v":"8:4"}],"sourceClass":"sn-ref","t":"span"}," ",{"c":["human beings"],"sourceClass":"sn-excerpt","t":"span"}," (literally ",{"c":["son of Adam"],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"},"): The Hebrew idiom ",{"c":["son of man"],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"}," (or ",{"c":["son of Adam"],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"},") means a human being. Through the influence of ",{"href":"?bref=Dan.7.13-14","r":"Dan.7.13-14","rawR":"Dan.7.13-14","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Dan.7.13-14","value":"Dan.7.13-14"}],"t":"ref","v":"Dan 7:13-14"},", it became a title with divine overtones in the New Testament. See ",{"href":"?bref=Heb.2.6-8","r":"Heb.2.6-8","rawR":"Heb.2.6-8","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Heb.2.6-8","value":"Heb.2.6-8"}],"t":"ref","v":"Heb 2:6-8"},", where this passage is quoted."],"sourceClass":"sn-text","t":"p"}],"id":"StudyNote:Ps.8.4","refs":[{"book":"PSA","endChapter":8,"endVerse":4,"startChapter":8,"startVerse":4}],"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Ps.8.4","product":"TyndaleOpenStudyNotes","typename":"StudyNote"},"sourceBookAppCode":"PSA","sourceChapterCoverage":[8],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"ddc783ed124296fb4b7b4c46e310036151fc12b26bda3959126738f9e6aeeecf","sourceItemName":"Ps.8.4","sourceMember":"Tyndale Open Study Notes/StudyNotes.xml","sourceOrder":6036,"sourceReferenceException":false,"sourceReferenceMappingEvidence":{"appCode":"PSA","canonicalOSIS":"Ps","method":"official_book_intro_ref_title","sourceOSIS":"Ps"},"sourceReferenceStatus":"canonical","sourceRefsExact":"Ps.8.4","sourceRelease":"1.25","sourceTitleExact":null,"supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[],"title":"Ps.8.4","type":"StudyNote"},{"chapterAssociationStatus":"canonical_reference","content":[{"c":[{"c":[{"href":"?bref=Ps.8.5","r":"Ps.8.5","rawR":"Ps.8.5","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.8.5","value":"Ps.8.5"}],"t":"ref","v":"8:5"}],"sourceClass":"sn-ref","t":"span"}," ",{"c":["Yet you made them only a little lower than God:"],"sourceClass":"sn-excerpt","t":"span"}," Humans bear God’s image; the Lord has endowed humans with dignity and charged them to rule (",{"href":"?bref=Gen.1.26-27","r":"Gen.1.26-27","rawR":"Gen.1.26-27","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Gen.1.26-27","value":"Gen.1.26-27"}],"t":"ref","v":"Gen 1:26-27"},"). ",{"href":"?bref=Heb.2.6-8","r":"Heb.2.6-8","rawR":"Heb.2.6-8","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Heb.2.6-8","value":"Heb.2.6-8"}],"t":"ref","v":"Hebrews 2:6-8"}," applies these words to Jesus Christ, the ideal human who fully realized God’s purposes."],"sourceClass":"sn-text","t":"p"}],"id":"StudyNote:Ps.8.5","refs":[{"book":"PSA","endChapter":8,"endVerse":5,"startChapter":8,"startVerse":5}],"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Ps.8.5","product":"TyndaleOpenStudyNotes","typename":"StudyNote"},"sourceBookAppCode":"PSA","sourceChapterCoverage":[8],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"4e9367b17f5fd47d3fa7ba1a109ec6ba10ae068a6775d41d4cc50d8d655a9523","sourceItemName":"Ps.8.5","sourceMember":"Tyndale Open Study Notes/StudyNotes.xml","sourceOrder":6037,"sourceReferenceException":false,"sourceReferenceMappingEvidence":{"appCode":"PSA","canonicalOSIS":"Ps","method":"official_book_intro_ref_title","sourceOSIS":"Ps"},"sourceReferenceStatus":"canonical","sourceRefsExact":"Ps.8.5","sourceRelease":"1.25","sourceTitleExact":null,"supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[],"title":"Ps.8.5","type":"StudyNote"},{"chapterAssociationStatus":"canonical_reference","content":[{"c":[{"c":[{"href":"?bref=Ps.8.6","r":"Ps.8.6","rawR":"Ps.8.6","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.8.6","value":"Ps.8.6"}],"t":"ref","v":"8:6"}],"sourceClass":"sn-ref","t":"span"}," ",{"c":["gave them charge of everything:"],"sourceClass":"sn-excerpt","t":"span"}," The psalmist is still referring to humans in general. Paul applies these words to Jesus as the perfect man who has made the created order—even death (",{"href":"?bref=1Cor.15.25-27","r":"1Cor.15.25-27","rawR":"1Cor.15.25-27","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Cor.15.25-27","value":"1Cor.15.25-27"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Cor 15:25-27"},")—subject to God and his glory. The New Testament connects these themes of creation and salvation with Jesus Christ (",{"href":"?bref=John.1.1-2","r":"John.1.1-2","rawR":"John.1.1-2","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"John.1.1-2","value":"John.1.1-2"}],"t":"ref","v":"John 1:1-2"},", ",{"href":"?bref=John.1.14","r":"John.1.14","rawR":"John.1.14","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"John.1.14","value":"John.1.14"}],"t":"ref","v":"14"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Col.1.16","r":"Col.1.16","rawR":"Col.1.16","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Col.1.16","value":"Col.1.16"}],"t":"ref","v":"Col 1:16"},")."],"sourceClass":"sn-text","t":"p"}],"id":"StudyNote:Ps.8.6","refs":[{"book":"PSA","endChapter":8,"endVerse":6,"startChapter":8,"startVerse":6}],"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Ps.8.6","product":"TyndaleOpenStudyNotes","typename":"StudyNote"},"sourceBookAppCode":"PSA","sourceChapterCoverage":[8],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"dfca2c773e7334d1aa399129f024ff66a3fea05901892501232e62e73b19d1ce","sourceItemName":"Ps.8.6","sourceMember":"Tyndale Open Study Notes/StudyNotes.xml","sourceOrder":6038,"sourceReferenceException":false,"sourceReferenceMappingEvidence":{"appCode":"PSA","canonicalOSIS":"Ps","method":"official_book_intro_ref_title","sourceOSIS":"Ps"},"sourceReferenceStatus":"canonical","sourceRefsExact":"Ps.8.6","sourceRelease":"1.25","sourceTitleExact":null,"supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[],"title":"Ps.8.6","type":"StudyNote"},{"chapterAssociationStatus":"canonical_reference","content":[{"c":[{"c":[{"href":"?bref=Ps.8.7-8","r":"Ps.8.7-8","rawR":"Ps.8.7-8","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.8.7-8","value":"Ps.8.7-8"}],"t":"ref","v":"8:7-8"}],"sourceClass":"sn-ref","t":"span"}," ",{"c":["Wild animals"],"sourceClass":"sn-excerpt","t":"span"},{"c":[","],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"}," including ",{"c":["birds"],"sourceClass":"sn-excerpt","t":"span"}," and ",{"c":["fish"],"sourceClass":"sn-excerpt","t":"span"},{"c":[","],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"}," remind readers of God’s creation of the animal world in ",{"href":"?bref=Gen.1.1-31","r":"Gen.1.1-31","rawR":"Gen.1.1-31","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Gen.1.1-31","value":"Gen.1.1-31"}],"t":"ref","v":"Gen 1"},". Contrary to beliefs among Israel’s neighbors in the ancient Near East, animals are not sacred."],"sourceClass":"sn-text","t":"p"}],"id":"StudyNote:Ps.8.7-8","refs":[{"book":"PSA","endChapter":8,"endVerse":8,"startChapter":8,"startVerse":7}],"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Ps.8.7-8","product":"TyndaleOpenStudyNotes","typename":"StudyNote"},"sourceBookAppCode":"PSA","sourceChapterCoverage":[8],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"05c59e2682f781c34714038c5af5314a4755537a2a05f64c47fda3119d39f33c","sourceItemName":"Ps.8.7-8","sourceMember":"Tyndale Open Study Notes/StudyNotes.xml","sourceOrder":6039,"sourceReferenceException":false,"sourceReferenceMappingEvidence":{"appCode":"PSA","canonicalOSIS":"Ps","method":"official_book_intro_ref_title","sourceOSIS":"Ps"},"sourceReferenceStatus":"canonical","sourceRefsExact":"Ps.8.7-8","sourceRelease":"1.25","sourceTitleExact":null,"supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[],"title":"Ps.8.7-8","type":"StudyNote"}],"version":"v2-a101d843a2f0cd3fc0c6"}